  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43340832",
      "title": "Performing Optimistic Updates With NextJS",
      "lectureOrder": 179,
      "videoOrder": 165,
      "sourceHash": "c2055781dd4ad78e384ede7df1c7d2d93a0b7036d0f3d0f135bafd33571257c6",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 2.25,
          "en": "Here in this application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.25,
          "end": 5.37,
          "en": "we would provide a better user experience",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 5.37,
          "end": 9.06,
          "en": "if we would immediately update this like status",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.06,
          "end": 13.11,
          "en": "even before it has been processed in the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.11,
          "end": 16.62,
          "en": "And that's a concept or a pattern",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.62,
          "end": 18.93,
          "en": "called optimistic updating,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 18.93,
          "end": 22.14,
          "en": "which in the end simply means that we're optimistic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.14,
          "end": 25.65,
          "en": "that our update will work, and therefore we wanna show",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.65,
          "end": 28.71,
          "en": "the new state immediately to the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 28.71,
          "end": 31.44,
          "en": "and perform the update behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.44,
          "end": 33.51,
          "en": "And then only if that update would fail",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 33.51,
          "end": 37.593,
          "en": "or something like this, we wanna roll back the update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.43,
          "end": 43.08,
          "en": "And React and Next.js make that simple and straightforward",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.08,
          "end": 45.96,
          "en": "because React provides another built-in hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.96,
          "end": 48.9,
          "en": "called useOptimistic, which you can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.9,
          "end": 52.02,
          "en": "to perform such optimistic updates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.02,
          "end": 54.93,
          "en": "And therefore that's a hook we'll use now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 54.93,
          "end": 58.23,
          "en": "For that, back in this posts.js file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.23,
          "end": 60.15,
          "en": "in the components folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 60.15,
          "end": 62.4,
          "en": "I wanna update my Posts here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 62.4,
          "end": 64.86,
          "en": "which I'm outputting optimistically",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 64.86,
          "end": 68.313,
          "en": "whenever the data for one of those posts changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.39,
          "end": 72.01,
          "en": "Now therefore I'll start by calling useOptimistic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 74.43,
          "end": 77.313,
          "en": "from inside this Posts component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.11,
          "end": 82.35,
          "en": "And I'm actually doing this here in the Posts component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 82.35,
          "end": 85.71000000000001,
          "en": "because it's actually the entire posts array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 85.71000000000001,
          "end": 89.88,
          "en": "that's being fetched from the database for this posts page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.88,
          "end": 92.88,
          "en": "And it's that entire list of posts that, in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.88,
          "end": 94.413,
          "en": "got updated therefore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 95.43,
          "end": 97.32,
          "en": "So here I'm calling useOptimistic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 97.32,
          "end": 101.88,
          "en": "but in order to call it we must import this hook from React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 101.88,
          "end": 104.43,
          "en": "So here at the top of the file you should",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 104.43,
          "end": 109.43,
          "en": "import { useOptimistic } from 'react'",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 110.4,
          "end": 111.233,
          "en": "Like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 113.55,
          "end": 116.25,
          "en": "Now with that, we can call useOptimistic here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 116.25,
          "end": 117.6,
          "en": "in the Posts component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 117.6,
          "end": 120.6,
          "en": "And this hook now takes a couple of inputs",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 120.6,
          "end": 122.82,
          "en": "and gives us a couple of outputs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.82,
          "end": 127.26,
          "en": "The first input it takes is the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 127.26,
          "end": 128.88,
          "en": "with which we wanna start.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 128.88,
          "end": 131.06,
          "en": "So, the data we fetched from the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 131.06,
          "end": 133.053,
          "en": "In this case the post array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 133.95,
          "end": 137.64,
          "en": "That's the first argument you should pass to useOptimistic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.581,
          "end": 141.51,
          "en": "The second argument is a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.51,
          "end": 144.6,
          "en": "that will be called automatically by React in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.6,
          "end": 146.55,
          "en": "when you tell it to call it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.55,
          "end": 149.49,
          "en": "and you'll see how that works in just a second,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.49,
          "end": 152.853,
          "en": "that will update this posts array optimistically.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 153.93,
          "end": 155.07,
          "en": "So this will be a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 155.07,
          "end": 158.16,
          "en": "that changes this post array on the client side",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 158.16,
          "end": 162.09,
          "en": "until the change has been processed on the server side,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 162.09,
          "end": 164.31,
          "en": "so that we can change it immediately,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.31,
          "end": 167.97,
          "en": "and then only sync it back with that server side state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 167.97,
          "end": 171.39,
          "en": "once that server site update has been performed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 171.39,
          "end": 175.26,
          "en": "For that, this function should then take two arguments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.26,
          "end": 180.26,
          "en": "where the first argument is the old posts states, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 180.51,
          "end": 183.57,
          "en": "So, for example, the initial array of posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 183.57,
          "end": 186.72,
          "en": "And the second argument is some data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 186.72,
          "end": 189.3,
          "en": "that allows us to perform the update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 189.3,
          "end": 191.7,
          "en": "And it will be up to us to define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 191.7,
          "end": 193.56,
          "en": "which kind of data we expect here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 193.56,
          "end": 198.349,
          "en": "In my case here, I expect to get the updatedPostId,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 198.349,
          "end": 200.94,
          "en": "so the ID of the post that should switch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 200.94,
          "end": 204.273,
          "en": "from liked to not liked, or vice versa.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 206.28,
          "end": 210.24,
          "en": "And then we need to add our logic for manipulating the posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 210.24,
          "end": 213.39,
          "en": "to this function body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 213.39,
          "end": 215.82,
          "en": "Now before we do that, let's talk about the things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 215.82,
          "end": 217.851,
          "en": "we get back from useOptimistic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 217.851,
          "end": 220.53300000000002,
          "en": "because that will be two elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 221.52,
          "end": 225.96,
          "en": "It will be an array with two elements, to be precise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 225.96,
          "end": 230.07,
          "en": "And the first element will be the updated posts array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 230.07,
          "end": 232.82999999999998,
          "en": "the optimistically updated post array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 232.82999999999998,
          "end": 235.15699999999998,
          "en": "and therefore I'll name it optimisticPosts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 238.2,
          "end": 242.7,
          "en": "The second argument will be a function which we can call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 242.7,
          "end": 245.49,
          "en": "to trigger that optimistic update.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 245.49,
          "end": 248.19,
          "en": "So to trigger this function, which we pass",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 248.19,
          "end": 251.223,
          "en": "as a second argument to useOptimistic, in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 252.36,
          "end": 255.337,
          "en": "And I'll call this updateOptimisticPosts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 257.55,
          "end": 259.533,
          "en": "Obviously these names are up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 262.02,
          "end": 265.83,
          "en": "We can then use the optimistic posts, instead of the posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 265.83,
          "end": 270.15,
          "en": "from the database, in all the places where we used posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 270.15,
          "end": 272.31,
          "en": "So for example here in this if check,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 272.31,
          "end": 275.013,
          "en": "and also here for looping through them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 276.9,
          "end": 279.693,
          "en": "And we'll soon call this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 280.77,
          "end": 283.40999999999997,
          "en": "For now, we will just assume that it is being called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 283.40999999999997,
          "end": 286.56,
          "en": "with the ID of the post for which the user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 286.56,
          "end": 289.14,
          "en": "changed the like status.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 289.14,
          "end": 291.09000000000003,
          "en": "And therefore now in this function body,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 291.09000000000003,
          "end": 294.45,
          "en": "we wanna update this posts array accordingly.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 294.45,
          "end": 298.47,
          "en": "And I'll start by getting the index of the post",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 298.47,
          "end": 301.11,
          "en": "that should be updated, so that should switch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 301.11,
          "end": 304.95,
          "en": "from liked to not liked, or the other way around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 304.95,
          "end": 308.64,
          "en": "And we can get that by taking a look at the previous posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 308.64,
          "end": 310.533,
          "en": "So the old posts array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 311.43,
          "end": 313.47,
          "en": "And call the findIndex method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 313.47,
          "end": 316.68,
          "en": "which is a default method built into JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 316.68,
          "end": 320.22,
          "en": "which executes a function on every item in that array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 320.22,
          "end": 323.4,
          "en": "And in that function we should return true or false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 323.4,
          "end": 326.46,
          "en": "And for that I'll compare the ID of every post",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 326.46,
          "end": 329.943,
          "en": "in that array to the updatedPostId here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 331.2,
          "end": 334.11,
          "en": "And if we got a match, it will give us the index",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 334.11,
          "end": 336.87,
          "en": "of that post in the previous posts array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 336.87,
          "end": 340.503,
          "en": "and that stands stored in this updatedPostIndex constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 342.03,
          "end": 345.45,
          "en": "Now it is possible that we don't find such a post,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 345.45,
          "end": 349.483,
          "en": "and therefore I'll check if updatedPostIndex is equal to -1,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 350.43,
          "end": 353.1,
          "en": "which is a value findIndex will return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 353.1,
          "end": 356.90999999999997,
          "en": "if it did not find a post for that condition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 356.90999999999997,
          "end": 358.56,
          "en": "And in that case I just wanna return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 358.56,
          "end": 360.393,
          "en": "the unchanged old posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 362.94,
          "end": 365.88,
          "en": "But if we make it past the safe check, we did find a post",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 365.88,
          "end": 366.99,
          "en": "that should be updated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 366.99,
          "end": 369.993,
          "en": "and I wanna update this in a immutable way now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 370.92,
          "end": 375.78,
          "en": "So I'll create an updatedPost, which is a new object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 375.78,
          "end": 380.78,
          "en": "into which I'll copy all the properties of the old post,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 381.09,
          "end": 384.78,
          "en": "which I'll get by accessing my previous posts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 384.78,
          "end": 386.58299999999997,
          "en": "for that updatedPostIndex.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 387.99,
          "end": 390.54,
          "en": "So that will give me access to one specific post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 390.54,
          "end": 392.37,
          "en": "And I'll spread all the properties",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 392.37,
          "end": 394.803,
          "en": "of that post into a new object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 397.17,
          "end": 400.23,
          "en": "Then I'll change that updatedPost,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 400.23,
          "end": 402.81,
          "en": "and set the likes property, which is the number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 402.81,
          "end": 405.42,
          "en": "of likes this post has, which I'm not using here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 405.42,
          "end": 408.09000000000003,
          "en": "but which I still get from the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 408.09000000000003,
          "end": 412.5,
          "en": "I'll set that to the updatedPost.likes we had.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 412.5,
          "end": 415.59000000000003,
          "en": "And then it depends on whether the post was liked before",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 415.59000000000003,
          "end": 418.23,
          "en": "or not, because I either want to deduct",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 418.23,
          "end": 420.93,
          "en": "the value or add a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 420.93,
          "end": 424.95,
          "en": "So I'll check if the updatedPost.isLiked is true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 424.95,
          "end": 428.28,
          "en": "And if that's the case, I wanna deduct the value,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 428.28,
          "end": 431.43,
          "en": "because it was liked and now it's not liked anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 431.43,
          "end": 434.58,
          "en": "So I want to reduce the number of likes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 434.58,
          "end": 436.533,
          "en": "Otherwise I want to add a like.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 439.35,
          "end": 442.77,
          "en": "And, more importantly for our application here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 442.77,
          "end": 446.31,
          "en": "I of course also wanna set the isLiked property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 446.31,
          "end": 450.84,
          "en": "for a given post to the opposite of what it was,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 450.84,
          "end": 455.84000000000003,
          "en": "with help of the exclamation mark operator, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 456.21,
          "end": 458.67,
          "en": "This will make sure that we switch it from liked",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 458.67,
          "end": 461.013,
          "en": "to not liked, or the other way around.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 139,
          "start": 462.84000000000003,
          "end": 465.09000000000003,
          "en": "And then I'll create a newPosts array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 140,
          "start": 465.09000000000003,
          "end": 468.21,
          "en": "where I copy all my old posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 141,
          "start": 468.21,
          "end": 472.69100000000003,
          "en": "And I wanna overwrite the post at this updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 142,
          "start": 472.69100000000003,
          "end": 476.55,
          "en": "postIndexPosition with my updated post.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 143,
          "start": 476.55,
          "end": 480.72,
          "en": "That would be an immutable way of creating a new posts array",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 144,
          "start": 480.72,
          "end": 483.693,
          "en": "with an updated post based on the old data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 145,
          "start": 487.17,
          "end": 489.33,
          "en": "And then here in this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 146,
          "start": 489.33,
          "end": 491.46,
          "en": "which we passed to useOptimistic,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 147,
          "start": 491.46,
          "end": 495.723,
          "en": "we should return that updated posts array.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 148,
          "start": 497.31,
          "end": 500.88,
          "en": "And React will then make that updated array available",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 149,
          "start": 500.88,
          "end": 504.69,
          "en": "through that optimisticPosts element it returns",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 150,
          "start": 504.69,
          "end": 507.273,
          "en": "in this array which is returned by useOptimistic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 151,
          "start": 508.92,
          "end": 511.47,
          "en": "So all we now have to do is make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 152,
          "start": 511.47,
          "end": 514.56,
          "en": "that we call updateOptimisticPosts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 153,
          "start": 514.56,
          "end": 519.03,
          "en": "and that we pass the ID of the post that should be updated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "start": 519.03,
          "end": 520.95,
          "en": "to this function in the end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "start": 520.95,
          "end": 523.713,
          "en": "so that it will be forwarded to this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 156,
          "start": 524.67,
          "end": 529.29,
          "en": "And we can do that by creating a new action here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 157,
          "start": 529.29,
          "end": 532.89,
          "en": "And for that I'll add a action function here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 158,
          "start": 532.89,
          "end": 535.23,
          "en": "And I'll name it updatePost.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 159,
          "start": 535.23,
          "end": 539.07,
          "en": "And I expect to get the postId as an argument here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 160,
          "start": 539.07,
          "end": 542.88,
          "en": "just as we did in our server action function before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 161,
          "start": 542.88,
          "end": 545.08,
          "en": "And in there I'll call updateOptimisticPosts",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 162,
          "start": 546.33,
          "end": 549.543,
          "en": "and forward the postId to this function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 163,
          "start": 550.59,
          "end": 552.27,
          "en": "And that's now, of course, the function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 164,
          "start": 552.27,
          "end": 555.12,
          "en": "provided by that useOptimistic hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 165,
          "start": 555.12,
          "end": 559.63,
          "en": "And thereafter, I wanna call my togglePostLikeStatus",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 166,
          "start": 561.96,
          "end": 565.233,
          "en": "function, and also pass the postId to that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 167,
          "start": 568.35,
          "end": 571.29,
          "en": "And in order to use await here, we should use async here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 168,
          "start": 571.29,
          "end": 574.11,
          "en": "And by adding async here, we'll also be able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 169,
          "start": 574.11,
          "end": 579.11,
          "en": "to use this even though I did not add \"use server\" here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 170,
          "start": 579.24,
          "end": 582.78,
          "en": "But Next.js does allow us to also set functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 171,
          "start": 582.78,
          "end": 586.77,
          "en": "like this as client actions, therefore if they have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 172,
          "start": 586.77,
          "end": 588.87,
          "en": "async in front of them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 173,
          "start": 588.87,
          "end": 592.14,
          "en": "So now it's this updatePost function that should be passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 174,
          "start": 592.14,
          "end": 594.54,
          "en": "to this post component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 175,
          "start": 594.54,
          "end": 597.66,
          "en": "So there we, for example, should add an action prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 176,
          "start": 597.66,
          "end": 599.88,
          "en": "though the name of this prop is up to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 177,
          "start": 599.88,
          "end": 601.503,
          "en": "because it's your component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 178,
          "start": 603,
          "end": 606.87,
          "en": "But you should pass updatePost as a value to that prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 179,
          "start": 606.87,
          "end": 610.08,
          "en": "And then, in that component we should accept",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 180,
          "start": 610.08,
          "end": 613.41,
          "en": "that action prop, or whatever you named it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 181,
          "start": 613.41,
          "end": 617.37,
          "en": "and use that as a value for this form action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 182,
          "start": 617.37,
          "end": 620.64,
          "en": "And you still should bind the post ID",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 183,
          "start": 620.64,
          "end": 622.533,
          "en": "because we still need that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 184,
          "start": 623.4,
          "end": 627.45,
          "en": "But with that, we now again got an extra intermediate",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 185,
          "start": 627.45,
          "end": 630.09,
          "en": "form action that will be executed first,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 186,
          "start": 630.09,
          "end": 632.61,
          "en": "and that will trigger our optimistic update,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 187,
          "start": 632.61,
          "end": 634.77,
          "en": "and also make sure that we trigger",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 188,
          "start": 634.77,
          "end": 636.75,
          "en": "that server action behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 189,
          "start": 636.75,
          "end": 638.79,
          "en": "But thanks to this optimistic update,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 190,
          "start": 638.79,
          "end": 641.01,
          "en": "the UI should update immediately,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 191,
          "start": 641.01,
          "end": 644.04,
          "en": "and then the server action still does its thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 192,
          "start": 644.04,
          "end": 647.13,
          "en": "and React and Next.js will then sync everything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 193,
          "start": 647.13,
          "end": 650.04,
          "en": "thereafter once the server action is done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 194,
          "start": 650.04,
          "end": 653.1,
          "en": "That's how you can think about that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 195,
          "start": 653.1,
          "end": 656.1,
          "en": "So with that, if you save that all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 196,
          "start": 656.1,
          "end": 657.78,
          "en": "you'll see we get an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 197,
          "start": 657.78,
          "end": 661.863,
          "en": "that useOptimistic only works in client components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 198,
          "start": 662.97,
          "end": 664.41,
          "en": "Well, that's no problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 199,
          "start": 664.41,
          "end": 667.71,
          "en": "We can simply add \"use client\" at the top here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 200,
          "start": 667.71,
          "end": 671.22,
          "en": "because the only server action we're using in that file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 201,
          "start": 671.22,
          "end": 673.413,
          "en": "is defined in a separate file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 202,
          "start": 674.85,
          "end": 677.88,
          "en": "So we can add \"use client\" without problems here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 203,
          "start": 677.88,
          "end": 680.13,
          "en": "at the top of this file that holds",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 204,
          "start": 680.13,
          "end": 682.11,
          "en": "the post and posts components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 205,
          "start": 682.11,
          "end": 685.26,
          "en": "And with that saved, we can reload again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 206,
          "start": 685.26,
          "end": 686.73,
          "en": "we can see our posts.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 207,
          "start": 686.73,
          "end": 689.13,
          "en": "And now if I unlike that, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 208,
          "start": 689.13,
          "end": 691.47,
          "en": "you see it's immediately unliked.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 209,
          "start": 691.47,
          "end": 694.02,
          "en": "If I like it, it's immediately liked here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 210,
          "start": 694.02,
          "end": 697.41,
          "en": "And we don't have to wait for that server action to finish.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 211,
          "start": 697.41,
          "end": 700.293,
          "en": "And that's optimistic updating in action.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
